      "content": "To address signal leakage and authentication without raising red flags, consider incorporating \"ambient verification\" methods that don't rely on traditional cryptographic handshakes. One approach is to utilize \"social engineering\" tactics, such as pre-arranged, cryptic phone numbers or email addresses that only the authorized recipient would recognize. You could also use \"watermarking\" techniques, where a unique identifier is embedded in the message that can only be deciphered by the intended recipient, perhaps through a custom-built application or a one-time password. Another option is to leverage \"human-in-the-loop\" authentication, where the recipient is required to confirm their identity through a manual process, such as a coded message or a pre-arranged phrase.",
